// The long tail: every other powered thing a scan might find.
//
// The hand-curated catalog (devices.ts, devices-extra.ts) covers the loads that
// dominate a school or office in detail. This table covers everything else a
// camera can see with a plug on it - 1109 devices, 2281 names a model might use for
// them - so a reading of "air fryer" or "label maker" is priced instead of being
// dropped. Each row is a device's typical running and standby draw (U.S. DOE
// Energy Saver appliance table, ENERGY STAR data and manufacturer nameplates);
// its family supplies the group, icon, duty cycle and a realistic fix. The band
// around each figure is deliberately wide, and a model's own watt reading for the
// unit it sees is blended in (lib/estimate.ts), as for every other device.
//
// Generated; edit the data, not the shape.

